    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily into a soft matchup against Gibson, with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our strongest play at a 74.74. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a respectable 4.01 xERA in Soriano, his elite skill set and the +14% boost from a favorable platoon matchup anchor our lineup. Following closely, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.25) and **Josh Lowe** (69.57) provide significant value; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a strong BvP track record (42 PA) against Nola, while **Josh Lowe** is a prime candidate to exploit the high-xERA Gibson, despite the efficiency drag from batting in the 8-hole. **Nolan Schanuel** also registers as an elite play (64.83) at the UTIL spot, leveraging a lead-off advantage to capitalize on Gibson\u2019s poor expected ERA.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Jacob Wilson**, whose 57.24 score hovered just outside the cut-off for the starting nine. While **Jacob Wilson** features a favorable wind-out condition (+5%) and solid SP skill metrics, the optimizer ultimately favored the higher-floor efficiency of our active core, particularly given the confirmed batting orders for **Sam Antonacci** and **Nolan Schanuel**. We are closely monitoring the lineup status of **Jacob Wilson**, as his \"Lineup Pending\" designation introduces enough variance to keep him on the pine in favor of the finalized production expected from **Denzer Guzman** and **Wade Meckler**, both of whom are positioned to maximize the Gibson matchup. \n\nRisks for today include the potential for suppressed production for **Andy Pages** (49.10), as he faces a challenging 3.23 xERA from Ryan, necessitating a high-volume effort to justify his slot. Similarly, while **Jackson Merrill** holds a decent score of 53.04, his negative platoon split against P\u00e9rez is a point of concern. We continue to hold high-upside assets like **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Cole Carrigg** in reserve, prepared to pivot if late-breaking weather or lineup changes shift the 5x5 landscape. We remain hyper-focused on SB opportunities today, as any deviation in projected sprint speed relative to opposing battery efficiency will dictate our mid-game pinch-hit maneuvers.",
